      "claim": "Glass is a brittle material that can shatter under sufficient impact, and steel, while strong, is not indestructible.",
      "evidence": "Materials science references (e.g., ASTM standards) describe glass as having low tensile strength and steel as having high but finite yield strength.",
      "weight": 0.30,
